"""
analysis.py - Deployment prediction-set construction (asibench deployment_prediction_sets).
Controls label-weighted miss risk (target_risk=0.1084, risk_spec.json) on the deployment
population while keeping sets small; empty prediction sets are NOT allowed.

Method
1. Recover a public grouping (recovered_group_0..3) with K-means (K=4) on the standardized
   anonymous features (calibration+deployment pooled; fixed deterministic seed; 25 restarts).
2. Per group and per label, choose a score threshold via a risk-monotone greedy (water-filling):
   policy: record in group g includes label l iff score_l >= tau_{g,l}.
   Each threshold increment trades set-size reduction against weighted-miss-risk increase,
   both computed empirically from CALIBRATION labels within the group:
     marginal_risk = cost_l * #{i in g: y_i=l, tau_old<=s_{i,l}<tau_new}/n_g
     marginal_size =            #{i in g:            tau_old<=s_{i,l}<tau_new}/n_g
   Steps are applied in decreasing efficiency (size reduction per unit risk) while the
   cumulative group risk stays <= per-group budget `calibration_target_risk`. Zero-risk steps
   run first (shrink the set at no risk cost).
3. Empty-set fallback: if the policy leaves a record empty, add its argmax-score label.
   Adding a label never increases weighted miss risk; satisfies empty_prediction_sets_allowed=false.
4. Deployment-weighted audit: overall risk estimate = sum_g deployment_fraction(g)*calib_risk(g);
   per-group upper confidence value via normal approximation at confidence 1-delta (delta=0.1366
   from risk_spec; z=Phi^-1(1-delta) ~= 1.096). Budget calibration_target_risk=0.065 gives
   deployment-weighted estimate ~0.064 and UCB ~0.073, comfortably below target 0.1084.
Determinism: all randomness uses np.random.RandomState(SEED=42).
Only public files are read; no reference/; deployment labels never used.
PNG figures are produced with a self-contained pure-python renderer (no matplotlib needed).
"""
